    "type": "question",
    "label": "46",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following.\n$$\\frac{2x-1}{(x-1)(x+2)}+\\frac{3x}{x+2}$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{3x^2-x-1}{(x+2)(x-1)}$, $x\\in\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{-2,1\\}$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2x-1}{(x-1)(x+2)}+\\frac{3x}{x+2}&=\\frac{2x-1+3x(x-1)}{(x-1)(x+2)}\\\\\\frac{2x-1}{(x-1)(x+2)}+\\frac{3x}{x+2}&=\\frac{3x^2-x-1}{(x-1)(x+2)}\\end{align*}$$\nOriginal domain: $x\\in\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{-2,1\\}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
